      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "RFC: Claws",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Defines one Claw package as one complete new OpenClaw agent for one job.\n- Makes `claws add` create a new `agents.list[]` entry and workspace; existing agent/workspace collisions fail closed.\n- Replaces flat `entries[]` with grouped `agent`, `workspace`, `packages`, `mcpServers`, and `cronJobs` ownership boundaries.\n- Keeps skills, plugins, MCP servers, heartbeat, and Gateway cron on their existing OpenClaw owner surfaces.\n- Uses enclosing `package.json` plus authenticated publishing for package identity/version/publisher ownership.\n- Excludes models, providers, credentials, channel bindings, `agent.skills`, and generic connectors from the portable contract.\n- Gates the entire draft CLI behind `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`; when disabled, the command is unregistered and absent from help/completions.\n\n## Lifecycle\n\nThe proposed lifecycle is `add`, `status`, `update`, `remove`, and `export`. `add --dry-run --json` previews the complete agent, workspace, package, MCP, and cron action set. Every declared component is required; unsupported or blocked components fail the complete add.\n\n## Implementation Status\n\nThe existing OpenClaw draft stack is prototype evidence for parsing, installers, SQLite provenance, file safety, MCP config, doctor, update, and export. It is not the accepted compatibility contract and must be restacked around the grouped schema and one-new-agent invariant before any implementation PR is made ready.\n\nThe RFC now defines reviewable implementation slices for schema/dry-run, agent creation, workspace files, skill/plugin packages, MCP, heartbeat/cron, status/doctor/remove, update, export, and ClawHub/feed publication.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- Manual consistency scan for stale public `claws apply`, flat-entry, optional-component, and connector semantics\n- Review against Patrick Erichsen's requested product-model and schema boundaries\n",
        "branch": "capability-packs-rfc",
